  "security_implications": "This module decodes a debug policy bus and generates enable signals for three debug categories (2,3,4). The valid and relocked status use MuBi4 multi-bit encoding to resist single-bit faults, while the category field is unprotected. cat4_dbg_o is not gated by relocked, potentially allowing permanent highest-privilege debug access even when the system is locked. SampleValidOnce=0 enables continuous sampling, making the category vulnerable to post-authentication changes. Faults on the unprotected category could stealthily elevate debug privileges. These issues affect the SoC debug access control and, if exploited, could allow unauthorized debugging and security boundary breach.",
